{
  "_about": "Voice commands. Say the prefix, then a command: \"Computer, scroll down\". The prefix only counts at the start of what you say, so a sentence that merely contains the word is typed as usual. To change anything, copy this file to %APPDATA%\\VoiceOS\\commands.json and edit that copy; it replaces this one. 'phrases' are what Voiceitt writes when you say the command (English). 'number' is what the user can say instead of the words (\"Computer, 43\"); the first digit is the group. Numbers must match exactly and must be unique. 'group' is the heading the command is listed under in the command panel, which shows the first phrase. 'hebrew' is reserved for the Hebrew engine and not used yet. To point 'open mail' (or browser, terminal) at the right program without editing: open the program, pick it as the dictation window, and say \"Computer, this is my mail\".",
  "prefixes": [ "computer" ],
  "commands": [
